{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/807804-homebrew-nosferatu-bloodline-wytch-discipline","id":807804,"title":"Homebrew Nosferatu Bloodline: Wytch & Discipline","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-13T05:54:12-08:00","id":807804,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Homebrew Nosferatu Bloodline: Wytch & Discipline","content":"This is a little rough around the edges and needs some work I think. Interested to hear your feedback.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline: Wytch<br /> Parent Clan: Nosferatu<br /> Bloodline Disciplines: Vigor, Nightmare, Celerity<br /> Gift: Wytch Fire Devotion Set. Wytch's are immune to their own individual fire, another Wytch's fire can harm them.<br /> Bane: Bane of Fire: </b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Because Wytch have grown used to their own &quot;fire&quot; when confronted with true fire a Wytch must make a Fear Frenzy check which is capped by humanity and suffers a negative 1.</span><br /> <br /> <b>History.</b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Wytch bloodline has been around for many hundred of years but was largely unknown until the days of the Salem Witch Hunts, Massachusetts in 1692.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">The bloodline rose to prominence during the early days of the Witch Hunt where they Ghouled and bestowed upon many people the power of their spiritual fire, </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">this however had major repercussions because of the highly superstitious and corrupt populous, it is because of this bloodline that the Witch Hunt kicked off in full swing.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u200bThe Wytch's of the area immediately fled the area, lest they be discovered themselves and be united with their greatest fear, true fire.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Appearance.</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Kindred of the Wytch Bloodline come in many different shapes and sizes and there for it is almost impossible to tell them from other Nosferatu, however they do have a few</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">major tells, those tells being: Bright almost Fluorescent green eyes, pallid olive skin and extremely boney features. </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>New Devotion: Wytch Fire.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Nosferatu of the Wytch bloodline have learnt to summon a bestial like green, this fire is spiritual in nature and is brought fourth from the beast of the kindred, it does not have the same affects on kindred as true fire would, meaning that when struck or in the presence of it, there is no need to check for frenzy and no need for any aggravated damage to be done by it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The Green Flame </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Dice pool: None<br /> Cost: 1 vitae<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> At this level of mastery the Wytch can summon the green flames and coat weapons in it, this adds +1L</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Wytch's fire is more than a simple flame they summon, it acts as a guide. A Wytch can see in perfect darkness as their inner fire gives them night vision, there vision does not waver in the face of damage and with an expenditure of 1 vitae a Wytch may see into all forms of Twilight. Their inner flames even halt entities possessing them by burning them out. The Green Wytch Fire can also burn those who would usually not be affected by attacks, ephemeral, twilight beings and strix suffer bashing from these flames and take damage to their willpower.<br /> <br /> This Devotion cost 0xp to learn.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Flame Strike<br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Vigor </span></b></span><b>\u25cf Celerity \u25cf</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Cost: 1 vitae</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Dice pool: None for activation. Dexterity + Athletics + Wytch Fire</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Action: Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">With this devotion the kindred may hurl green bolts of fire at his opponent.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">The fire can be thrown Strength + Athletics metres. This acts as +1L </span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Wytch's Gaze<br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Nightmare </span></span><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u25cf\u25cf</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Cost: 1 vitae<br /> Dice pool: None<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Once active it appears as if Green Flames are trying to escape the Kindreds body, his eyes burn bright green, the back of his throat lights up and green veins course across his skin, making the Kindred blinding to look at, all attackers, no matter how close or far suffer a -3 to attack him.<br /> <br /> This devotions costs 2 experiences to learn<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Conflageration </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Nightmare \u25cf\u25cf</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Cost: 1 vitae</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Dice Pool: None</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Action: Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Wytch makes eye contact with the victim and makes it appear as if they have suddenly been engulfed by an inferno of green flames.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">These visions seem real and feel real to the victim, although cause no real damage.<br /> This ability, triggers fear frenzy in kindred which causes the victim to reflexively resist the frenzy with Resolve + Composure.<br /> In mortals and other creatures this imparts the shaken condition as above this is reflexively resisted with a Resolve + Composure.<br /> <br /> this Devotion cost 2 experiences to learn.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The Wytch King </b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Vigor \u25cf\u25cf</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Cost: 1 Vitae/ Turn<br /> Dice pool: None<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> Duration: Until Next Turn</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Wytch engulfs himself in his own cold burning fire, turning him into a walking inferno of green flames, whilst active all physical attacks the kindred makes are +1L, if physically attacked or grappled by an opponent the opponent suffers +2L .<br /> <br /> this Devotion cost 2 experiences to learn.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10405-lithiumdhalia","user":"LithiumDhalia","date":".  updated things 01-14-2016, 07:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10405-lithiumdhalia","name":"LithiumDhalia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T05:57:11-08:00","id":807807,"title":"","content":"I still have to add the dramatic failure and success stuff","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10405-lithiumdhalia","name":"LithiumDhalia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T07:51:14-08:00","id":807873,"title":"","content":"Changed the discipline to a devotion set under the advisement of a friend","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10405-lithiumdhalia","name":"LithiumDhalia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T00:57:24-08:00","id":808506,"title":"","content":"So the bane makes them more susceptible to actual fire.. why then do they possess Resilience? Especially when the Resilience devotion sounds more like Vigor (providing power into the Wytch Fire) .<br /> <br /> Similar question to Majesty? What's the point of Majesty there? It seems that whatever's being done by Majesty here could as well be done by Nightmare (ooking at Wytch's Gaze)<br /> <br /> It would also be worthwhile to mention that their fire is not actual fire. Also, it's worthwhile to consider what happens when two Wytch'es fight. <br /> <br /> It feels to me that the bloodline is trying to be too much at once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T04:12:43-08:00","id":808568,"title":"","content":"It's still a work in progress and I have some trouble matching themes for devotions. <br /> As for the fire, it is mentioned that it isn't metaphysically the same as real fire and it also says that their own fire can't affect them, meaning the individuals own fire cant, maybe I should clarify that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10405-lithiumdhalia","name":"LithiumDhalia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T04:38:17-08:00","id":808578,"title":"","content":"And I am commenting precisely because it's a work in progress <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So don't take anything I say personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T05:12:28-08:00","id":808588,"title":"","content":"I won't, I'm a Uni student so I am fairly used to it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid"